# A kernel that fails while frames are staged (D[async-output], #113).
# Once a kernel has failed, the driver returns the error of the context for
# every event, also for those whose copies had arrived before, and still
# runs a function of the host enqueued behind copies that never ran; so the
# stream of copies has the device write a mark into pinned memory after
# each staging's copies, which it does not do after the failure. The runtime
# ends the process with abort at a failure of the driver, and first has the
# thread of the frames write those whose marks have landed. The thread of
# the frames holds each write back by 2 s, longer than the driver takes to
# report a trap, so the frames are still queued when the run meets it.
#
# After: MDRT_FAULT_AFTER_FRAMES=2 makes a kernel trap after the copies of
# the 2nd frame (step 20) have arrived. Both frames are written, the frames
# of the reference to the byte, and the run ends with the report of the
# runtime at its own next call, once, which names the last kernel launched.
#
# Before: MDRT_FAULT_BEFORE_COPY=3 makes a kernel trap after the copies of
# the first 2 frames have arrived and before those of the 3rd (step 30),
# which never run. The 2 frames are written and the 3rd is not; a run whose
# frames had no thread would have written it before the fault, but its
# copies were not on the host when the kernel failed.
#
# Without a periodic cell the call of a frame waits for its own copies
# (D142): with MDRT_FAULT_BEFORE_COPY=3 that wait meets the failure, and the
# runtime reports it as the wait's, the frames of steps 5 and 10 written.
#
# MDIR_FRAME_COPY_FAIL=30 takes the wait of the thread for the copies of the
# frame of step 30 as failed, with the device well: the frames of steps 10
# and 20 are written, that of 30 and those queued after it are not, and the
# call of the next frame hands the error to the runtime, which reports it
# once and ends the process. Without a cell, the same error of the frame of
# step 10 is reported rather than the spread that the frame of step 25
# meets while the thread still holds it.
#
# REQUIRES: cuda
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && split-file %S/no-cell.test %t
# RUN: sed -e 's|Inputs/|%S/Inputs/|' \
